            <ArticleTitle>Partial aortic root remodeling with an adventitial inversion technique for an acute type a aortic dissection.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>327-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/j.1540-8191.2010.01002.x</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This case report describes a partial aortic root remodeling, which applied a valve-sparing technique, with an adventitial inversion technique for an acute type A aortic dissection with intimal tear extending into the noncoronary sinus of Valsalva. Postoperative computed tomography at six months showed no dissection or pseudoaneurysm in the aortic root.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
